# Zero-setup profile: nothing external runs. Good for the UI, auth, and the read-side (sections,
# week days). NOT the live board flow: under CFB_DEMO_PROFILE=memory each capability writes to its
# OWN private in-process pglite and publishes to a dead-end in-memory broker, so a proposed or
# scheduled session never reaches the board. To see sessions land on the board, use `npm run
# start:pg` (Postgres + RabbitMQ share one event log + one bus). See README.
CFB_PROFILE=local
CFB_DB=memory
CFB_DEMO_PROFILE=memory
RELAY_INTERVAL_MS=1000

STATIC_ROOT=public
PORT=3001
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001
